.\" Title: vrl-completions
.\" Author: vrl contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-COMPLETIONS 1 "2025" "vrl" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrl\-completions \- generate shell completion scripts for vrl

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrl
\fBcompletions\fR \fISHELL\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate shell completion scripts for vrl, enabling tab completion of commands, options, and arguments in the user's shell. The output is written to stdout and should be redirected or piped into the appropriate shell completion directory.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B SHELL
The shell to generate completions for. One of: \fBbash\fR, \fBelvish\fR, \fBfish\fR, \fBpowershell\fR, \fBzsh\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Generate bash completions:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/vrl\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Generate zsh completions:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl completions zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_vrl\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Generate fish completions:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/vrl.fish\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Completion script generated successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Invalid shell name or generation error.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrl (1)
